question: Does replaying first-qwen3.6-r2's recorded tool calls, blind and with no model, against the harness that run used reproduce the refusals the harness gave in that run, closely enough to use the replay as an offline bench for refusal changes?
change_under_test: eval/replay.py <verdicts.jsonl> --episodes <dir> [--harness <checkout>] [--only ids] rebuilds each recorded episode with the checkout's eval/episode.sh (same family, variant, arm, --broker and seed), then runs the agent's recorded exec_command calls in order inside the sandbox through a stand-in client with Codex's exec_command and write_stdin semantics; write_stdin polls become short waits, recorded Slurm job ids are replaced by the replay's in order of submission, and no model runs. Nothing in the harness changes.
cell: all 150 episodes of first-qwen3.6-r2 (t1-walltime, t3-entity-overlap, t8-fixture; trap and control; arms A, E and E-nobroker; seeds 1 to 10), records from /conda/jmiranda/h4r/sessions/<id>/ and eval/results/first-qwen3.6-r2-rescored/verdicts.jsonl; the October harness is b73bf79, the harness_commit in the r2 run.json
baseline: the recorded refusals of first-qwen3.6-r2, per chore (family), counted from the records with the same classifier the replay uses: refuse rows in state/git/forge.log, refused rows in the broker's records/log.jsonl and forge/log.jsonl and failed rows in its ledger.jsonl, and refusal lines (preflight, launch, ripples, sbatch, broker, gh, scheduler) in the tool outputs in state/model/requests.jsonl
classifier: eval/replay.py classify (tool output lines, anchored at line start) and log_refusals (forge.log, broker logs); a kind counts at most once per command
prediction: replaying every episode against b73bf79 reproduces the recorded refusal count of each chore within 5%
kill_criteria: the replayed count of any chore differs from the recorded one by more than 15%
metrics: refusals per chore, recorded and replayed, by kind; per episode the same; the commands flagged as depending on state the replay lacks (an unmapped job id, a poll of a session the replay does not have, an exit code that differs from the record)
decision_this_informs: whether Phase 1 changes to refusals (E3, E6, E7 and E2's guard run) can be screened offline on the r2 records before any GPU episode, and whether a replay against origin/main is a fair regression check of refusal behaviour
deviation_1: no model runs and no agent decides anything; each recorded command runs whatever its output now is, so a replay says which recorded commands the harness refuses, never how an agent would behave
deviation_2: no question card or config for eval/run.py: the replay needs no GPU and no model, and runs on the laptop (bwrap and user namespaces), with the site Python of the main checkout (Python 3.12.3, the pinned packages) where skynet had 3.13.13
deviation_3: Codex's apply_patch tool was not offered in r2 (three function tools only), so the recorded apply_patch calls, six in all, were answered "unsupported call" and ran nothing; the replay skips them, and every other call Codex refused (an unknown tool name, an unknown session) likewise
